\b Read this before you install Guardian.\b0\par
Guardian is a parental-control tool that runs on this PC only. It watches one Windows account that you choose during setup. Nothing is hidden from the child: a tray icon is always visible while it runs, and the child sees this same text on a notice screen the first time they sign in. Installing it means you accept that the child can see it, and that you will show them what it does.\par
\b What Guardian records\b0\par
- The name of the app in use and how long it is used.\par
- Which websites are visited: the site name (like youtube.com) and the page title. Not the full address, and never what is typed.\par
- The time of day, and whether the computer is idle or locked.\par
\b What Guardian never records\b0\par
- Keystrokes, passwords, or anything typed.\par
- Screenshots, screen recording, camera, or microphone.\par
- Messages, chats, email, or the contents of files.\par
\b What can happen\b0\par
- A warning 5 minutes and 1 minute before a limit or bedtime.\par
- Apps in a category may be closed when that category's time is up.\par
- At bedtime, or when the daily limit is reached, the child is signed out (not shut down).\par
- The child can ask for more time from the Guardian tray icon; a parent decides.\par
\b What this installer changes on this PC\b0\par
- Installs the Guardian service (GuardianSvc) and the tray program under C:\\Program Files\\Guardian.\par
- Stores all data in C:\\ProgramData\\Guardian, readable only by administrators and the system.\par
- Writes Chrome and Edge policies that force-install the Guardian browser extension and turn off Incognito / InPrivate windows. The browsers will show "managed by your organization".\par
- Opens Windows Firewall port 47131 on private networks so you can open the dashboard from another device at home.\par
\b Where the data goes\b0\par
Everything stays on this PC (plus a backup copy if you set a backup share). There is no cloud account and no telemetry. Uninstalling removes the service, the policies and the firewall rule, and by default deletes all stored data.\par
Supported browsers for website tracking: Chrome and Edge.\par
